Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?raster:=20M1.1=20A3b=20=E2=80=94=20the=20real?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20PICA=20fragment=20semantics=20run=20on=20Metal?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

the test drives raster.frag+vert themselves (the rack's same GLSL
through prepare()) over the whole fragment pipeline with PICA
uniforms: the DYNAMIC=1 path reads tev/misc/units out of the Draw
block, the six combiner stages pass the vertex colour through, and
the two triangles' pixels come out the exact colours the vertices
carried — green left, red right, the letterbox navy round them.

the keys to this landing:
- prepare(source, values, to_image) bakes the spec constants' values
  in from the pipeline key (constant_id N = the key word N), and the
  image variant moves its SSBO out of the image's binding;
- the per-entry-point binding map replaces fake_missing: the resource
  bindings verbatim, the samplers at their own slots, and the
  sizes_buffer (the Tables' runtime-sized array needs its host size
  slot) — the writer errors named every missing one until it was
  right;
- the whole thing verified with the Draw block's plain u32 words,
  with the combiner pass words 0x000F000F and a half-and-half vertex
  layout the way the hardware placement reads.

141 tests green; the MSL's [[buffer(N)]] attributes are in MSL text
where the writer laid them.
